\label{lem1}
    Let \(q\) be a prime and let \(\chi\) be a non-principal Dirichlet character modulo \(q\). Then, for every real \(t\), we have
    \[L\Big(\frac{1}{2}+\mathrm{i}t,\chi\Big) \ll (q(1+|t|))^{1/4}.\]

\label{lem2}
    Let \(\chi\) be a non-principal Dirichlet character modulo \(q\). Let \(a>1/2\) and set \(z=x+\mathrm{i} y\). Suppose that \(K(z)\) is holomorphic in the horizontal strip \(-a\le y \le 0\) satisfying the growth condition
    \[\max_{-a\le y \le 0}|K(x+\mathrm{i} y)| = O\Big(\frac{1}{(1+|x|)^2}\Big)\]
    as \(|x| \to \infty\). Then, we have, for every real \(t\),
    \begin{align*}
        \int_\mathbb{R} L\Big(\frac{1}{2}+\mathrm{i}t+\mathrm{i} u,\chi \Big)L\Big(\frac{1}{2}-\mathrm{i}t+\mathrm{i} u,\overline{\chi} \Big)K(u)\mathrm{d} u = \sum_{k,\ell \ge1}\frac{\chi(k)\overline{\chi}(\ell)}{\sqrt{k\ell}}\Big(\frac{\ell}{k}\Big)^{\mathrm{i}t}\widehat{K}(\log k\ell).
    \end{align*}

\label{lem3}
    Let $q$ be a prime and let $X\geq 2$. Then
\[\sum_{\substack{\chi(\bmod q)\\ \chi\neq\chi_0}}
\int_{-X}^{X} \Big|L \Big(\frac12+\mathrm{i}t,\chi\Big)\Big|^2 \mathrm{d} t \ll qX\log(qX).\]
